# Extension Rules

- Keep extension architecture compliant with Chrome Manifest V3.
- Do not introduce MV2-era patterns (persistent background pages, `background.html`).
- Keep docs in `docs/` rather than adding root markdown files beyond `README.md`.
- Preserve clear boundaries between content script, popup UI, and background/service-worker messaging.
- Follow least-privilege permissions in manifest updates; request only permissions/host access required for current functionality.
- Avoid unsafe runtime/script patterns (for example dynamic code execution) and keep extension messaging/input handling explicit and validated.
